--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, source-table producers, part 13: the set-up frame
--
--   `upF dA Z Z1 Cm body`: park the descriptor `dA → Z` (through `Z1`, counter `Cm`), push `0` on
--   the parameter registers `rg`, run D2's parameter phase `parP 0 0 0 0 Z`, run `body`, pop `rg`,
--   and park the descriptor back `Z → dA`. Theorem `upF_runs`: if `body` takes `RF v c₀` to
--   `RF v (extend ρS V c₀)` for every `v` satisfying `ParV` (`c₀` = the input with the descriptor
--   moved to `Z`), then `upF` takes `F` to `extend ρS V F` (the first half of `SetupS`).
